# Prim's Minimum Spanning Tree Algorithm

## 1. What Does Prim's Algorithm Do?

Prim's algorithm finds the **Minimum Spanning Tree (MST)** of a weighted, undirected graph.

A Minimum Spanning Tree:

- Connects every node
- Does not contain cycles
- Contains exactly `V - 1` edges
- Has the minimum possible total edge weight

---

## 2. Prim's Main Intuition

Prim's algorithm grows one connected tree.

> Start from any node and repeatedly choose the cheapest edge that connects the current tree to an unvisited node.

Unlike Kruskal, Prim does not sort all edges globally.

Instead, Prim maintains a group of nodes that are already part of the MST.

Initially:

```text
MST nodes = {0}
Outside   = {1, 2, 3}
```

Prim looks at all edges leaving the current MST and chooses the cheapest one that reaches an unvisited node.

The process continues until every node becomes part of the MST.

---

