# 24. Why Does Prim Not Need DSU?

Kruskal processes edges across the entire graph.

Therefore, it needs DSU to determine whether two endpoints already belong to the same component.

Prim grows one connected tree.

A node joins the tree only once.

Therefore, Prim uses:

```java
visited[node]
```

to determine whether a node has already joined the MST.

```text
Kruskal cycle prevention → DSU
Prim cycle prevention    → Visited array
```

