# 25. Prim vs Dijkstra in Code

Both algorithms may use:

```text
Adjacency list
PriorityQueue
Visited or distance arrays
```

But their heap values mean different things.

## Prim

```java
minHeap.offer(
    new int[]{edgeWeight, nextNode}
);
```

Meaning:

```text
Cheapest edge used to attach nextNode to the MST
```

## Dijkstra

```java
int newDistance =
    currentDistance + edgeWeight;
```

Meaning:

```text
Complete path cost from the source to nextNode
```

Remember:

```text
Prim:
Minimize the total cost of building the network.

Dijkstra:
Minimize path cost from one source.
```

