# 27. Important Interview Points

```text
1. Prim grows one connected tree.

2. It can start from any node.

3. A min-heap stores the available edges.

4. The heap returns the cheapest available connection.

5. A visited array prevents adding the same node twice.

6. A node may appear in the heap multiple times.

7. Old heap entries become stale after the node is visited.

8. A node is marked visited when it is removed from
   the heap, not when it is inserted.

9. Prim adds only the current edge weight, not the
   complete path cost.

10. The starting node is inserted with cost 0.

11. The starting node has no real parent.

12. If all nodes are not visited, the graph is disconnected.

13. The MST contains exactly V - 1 actual edges.

14. Prim usually uses an adjacency list, min-heap
    and visited array.
```

