# 29. Final Memory Trick

```text
START FROM ONE NODE
        ↓
PUSH ITS AVAILABLE EDGES
        ↓
REMOVE THE CHEAPEST EDGE
        ↓
IS THE NODE ALREADY VISITED?
       /                    \
     YES                     NO
      ↓                       ↓
    SKIP              ADD NODE TO MST
                              ↓
                    ADD CONNECTION COST
                              ↓
                    PUSH ITS UNVISITED
                         NEIGHBORS
                              ↓
                           REPEAT
```

The most important idea is:

> Prim repeatedly chooses the cheapest edge that expands the current MST to one new, unvisited node.

Short memory:

```text
Prim = Min-Heap + Adjacency List + Visited Array
```

And the most important coding rule is:

```java
if (visited[currentNode]) {
    continue;
}
```

This ensures that each node is added to the MST exactly once.
